From 112146020ac6e93c722dcd1c7e5d6dc9bd79cccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:08:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] soundwire: qcom: disable runtime PM on remove and gate
 the AHB clock only once

qcom_swrm_remove() gated the AHB ("iface") clock unconditionally, although
runtime suspend gates it too, and it left runtime PM enabled. Neither matters
while the controller is never unbound; it is now, on the ASUS Vivobook S 15
(X1E80100), whenever the ADSP restarts: the LPASS macros that clock the
controllers are unbound and probed again (see the q6dsp-lpass-clocks patches),
and the SoundWire controllers with them.

 - A controller that was runtime-suspended at that point (the usual case)
   got a second clk_disable_unprepare() on its macro's clock: unbalanced.
 - The next probe called pm_runtime_set_active() and pm_runtime_enable() on
   a device whose runtime PM was still enabled ("Unbalanced
   pm_runtime_enable!"), and a pending autosuspend could fire after remove
   without a driver. The device then counted as suspended while the new probe
   ran the bus with the clock enabled; the first runtime resume then enabled
   the clock again and, on the WCD938x buses, tried to take a running bus out
   of clock stop.

Disable runtime PM after the bus is deleted, gate the clock only if the
controller is active, and mark it suspended.

Not upstream.
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 6d8c81900..58978b4cc 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1751,7 +1751,12 @@ static void qcom_swrm_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev);
 
 	sdw_bus_master_delete(&ctrl->bus);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+
+	/* runtime suspend has gated the AHB clock already */
+	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pdev->dev))
+		clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
